# Contributing to {{ title }}

## The gate

```console
$ cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test
```

The same commands CI runs, so a green terminal means a green pull request.

`tests/protocol.rs` runs the built binary the way {{ host }} runs it and holds
the answers to what the host accepts - a plugin that passes its unit tests and
fails there is one {{ host }} would list and refuse.

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| `src/main.rs` | The manifest and the plugin's own work |
| `src/protocol.rs` | The wire: one call in on stdin, one reply out on stdout |
| `tests/protocol.rs` | The plugin run as the host runs it |
{{#source}}
| `src/requests.rs` | The requests {{ host }} asks on its own, and the rules a reply is held to |
| `src/source.rs` | Where the issues and the day's tasks come from |
| `tests/requests.rs` | Every request asked as the host asks it |
{{/source}}
| `assets/` | The mark's three master SVGs |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decisions, newest last |
